WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.509
Although the biggest movies these days seem
to be making more money than most small countries,

00:00:04.509 --> 00:00:06.880
that doesn't mean everyone is sharing in the
wealth.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:11.740
Sadly, quite a few 2019 movies — some with
big names and big budgets — have already

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:14.860
been given the thumbs down from critics and
audiences alike.

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.540
Here's why these 2019 films bombed at the
box office.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:23.420
Replicas is one of those science fiction/horror
movies that seems to exist solely to warn

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.200
the world's mad scientists that dead people
are supposed to stay that way.

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.710
Keanu Reeves plays Will Foster, a scientist
working on transferring the consciousnesses

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.560
of the dead into new bodies.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:37.540
After his wife and children are killed during
a boating trip, he enlists the help of a fellow

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:39.700
scientist to resurrect them via cloning.

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.520
Predictably, things quickly go wrong.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:46.750
Replicas performed dismally at the box office,
grossing just a little over $4 million, and

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:51.140
its aggregate Rotten Tomatoes score doesn't
suggest this was an under-hyped gem, either.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:55.719
Critics ripped the sci-fi thriller to pieces,
calling out its preposterous story, its numerous

00:00:55.719 --> 00:00:58.679
plot holes, and the squandering of its novel
potential.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.040
A number of critics have suggested that Reeves
was horribly miscast as a grieving genius,

00:01:03.140 --> 00:01:06.740
and more than one argued that Nicolas Cage
would've made a much better fit.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:11.470
Amidst a storm of unkind reviews of Replicas,
perhaps the best takedown of them all came

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.700
from The Los Angeles Times, which explained:

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:18.160
"The filmmakers manage to avoid every potentially
interesting choice for far dumber, and far

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.040
more inexplicable, conclusions."

00:01:21.340 --> 00:01:24.340
Don't worry, Joss Whedon fans: you haven't
missed anything important.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.600
2019's Serenity is a very different beast
indeed than the 2005 sci-fi cult classic.

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.600
"I am a leaf on the wind.

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:34.500
Watch how I soar."

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:39.600
No, this movie follows Baker Dill, the captain
of a fishing vessel who is dragged back into

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:43.680
his ex-wife Karen's life when she tries to
hire him to kill her current husband.

00:01:44.000 --> 00:01:45.620
So far, so straightforward, right?

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:47.120
Well, guess again.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:51.340
Because it is eventually revealed that Dill
is actually a character in a video game designed

00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:52.640
by a boy named Patrick.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:57.120
When Patrick's real-life mother remarried
an abusive man, he redesigned his game to

00:01:57.120 --> 00:01:59.120
be about destroying the new man in her life.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:03.860
Some critics praised a number of fine performances
that nevertheless failed to save an absurd

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:04.360
story.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:09.000
Most critics, however, agreed that Serenity's
script was horribly written — and its premise

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:10.260
was downright ludicrous.

00:02:10.670 --> 00:02:14.320
The biggest problem seems to have been the
film's poorly executed reveals, which The

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.860
Sunday Times called "shoddy narrative gimmicks."

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.420
Rather than adding depth or a fresh perspective
to the story, reviewers felt the twists were

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.560
"self-indulgent", while The Arts Desk wrote:

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.220
"It’s as if you’ve been watching a movie
which wasn’t that great to begin with, and

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:31.319
then the director crashes through the screen,
doubling up with laughter and telling you

00:02:31.320 --> 00:02:32.320
you’ve been had."

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:37.220
Louis Ashbourne Serkis plays a young boy in
present day England who stumbles upon the

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:42.580
legendary sword Excalibur in 2019's family-friendly
fantasy The Kid Who Would Be King.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.420
Unfortunately for Alex and his friends, King
Arthur's old enemy Morgana knows Excalibur

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:49.500
has been discovered and wants it for herself.

00:02:49.890 --> 00:02:53.860
Aided by the backwards-aging Merlin, Alex
and his friends embark on a quest to defeat

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:55.420
the dastardly sorceress.

00:02:55.550 --> 00:02:59.340
Sadly, their victory against the forces of
evil couldn't save the movie from grossing

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.300
just a little over half of its production
budget of $59 million.

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:08.970
Unlike most of the films that flopped in 2019,
The Kid Who Would Be King enjoyed mostly favorable

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:12.700
reviews, earning an impressive 90% score on
Rotten Tomatoes.

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:17.240
While writing about the film's inability to
turn a profit, Forbes placed part of the blame

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:21.710
on competing intellectual properties, pointing
out that Kid was forced to face off with films

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:24.640
like Aquaman and Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse.

00:03:24.880 --> 00:03:29.040
These movies featured characters audiences
were familiar with and wanted to see on the

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.480
big screen, whereas audiences simply struggled
to care about King Arthur and his friends.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:38.400
For a long time to come, the thing most people
may remember about the darkly comic revenge

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:42.300
thriller Cold Pursuit will be the interview
star Liam Neeson gave while promoting the

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:42.800
film.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:46.740
During this interview, Neeson revealed that,
in the wake of the sexual assault of a close

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:50.849
friend by a black man, he had once walked
the streets hoping any black man would start

00:03:50.849 --> 00:03:53.800
a fight with him so that Neeson could kill
him in retaliation.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.600
"It was horrible, horrible, and I think back
that I did that, and I’ve never admitted

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:01.420
that and I’m saying it to a journalist,
God forbid."

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:06.260
The interview sparked a firestorm of controversy,
eventually prompting an apology from the actor.

00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:11.160
Cold Pursuit's opening weekend pulled in $10.8
million — the lowest numbers for a Neeson

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.220
movie debut since 2010's The Next Three Days.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:19.260
Eventually, however, subsequent grosses helped
the film break even with its $60 million budget.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.340
It's impossible to know how much of that poor
performance was influenced by the response

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:27.460
to Neeson's colossal public blunder, though
according to some critics, there was plenty

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:31.220
in Cold Pursuit to dislike even if you'd never
heard his notorious interview.

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:36.340
Whether it was Neeson's interview or the film
itself that led to Cold Pursuit's chilly reception,

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:39.850
it's probably safe to say that it'll probably
be a while before Neeson is allowed to veer

00:04:39.850 --> 00:04:41.760
off-topic during a press interview.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:47.800
In the world of Captive State, 2019 is the
year aliens invade the Earth, ultimately leading

00:04:47.810 --> 00:04:52.550
to humanity's capitulation to the extraterrestrials
who rule the planet from their underground

00:04:52.550 --> 00:04:53.540
"Closed Zones."

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:57.900
A decade later, two brothers join a resistance
force against the aliens and find themselves

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:02.100
hunted by a shadowy Police Commander who has
dedicated himself to ending the resistance

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:03.220
once and for all.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:04.480
Or so it seems…

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.840
"No no no no.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.460
I’m going to watch it later.

00:05:09.960 --> 00:05:13.740
I’ve got it, mum's the word."

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:18.340
Captive State eventually grossed an unimpressive
$8.6 million worldwide.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.800
Overall, the movie's reviews agreed that the
plot was convoluted and that the film didn't

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.880
have the budget it needed to tell its story.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:30.000
Meanwhile, others felt the focus on the unwieldy
plot sacrificed believable characters.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:31.760
Reelviews's reviewer wrote:

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.440
"Characterization is perfunctory and unsatisfactory.

00:05:34.900 --> 00:05:37.260
We're watching a bunch of pawns on a filmmaker's
chessboard."

00:05:38.650 --> 00:05:44.460
A remake of a 2011 Spanish film with the same
name, 2019's Miss Bala stars Gina Rodriguez

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:45.780
of Jane the Virgin fame.

00:05:46.210 --> 00:05:50.900
The film brings Rodriguez to unfamiliar territory,
casting her as a Los Angeles make-up artist

00:05:50.919 --> 00:05:55.020
who trains to fight a Mexican drug cartel
after her friend is kidnapped during a trip

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:55.920
south of the border.

00:05:56.320 --> 00:06:00.699
While the casting of Rodriguez as an action
star may seem strange, most critics seemed

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:04.930
to agree it's just about the only thing that
ended up going right with Miss Bala — while

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:08.830
the rest of this would-be thriller is merely
a watered down, uninspired, and cardboard

00:06:08.830 --> 00:06:12.040
cutout version of the 2011 film it reimagines.

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:16.830
The Galveston Daily News wrote that Miss Bala
director Catherine Hardwicke "feels more like

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.240
a director for hire" than in her previous
films.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:24.240
No doubt partly as a result of all the negative
critical buzz, Miss Bala's gross barely broke

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:26.320
even with its $15 million budget.

00:06:26.780 --> 00:06:30.360
In spite of its poor performance critically,
a number of critics saved space to praise

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:32.500
Rodriguez's performance in their reviews.

00:06:32.760 --> 00:06:36.680
While agreeing that Miss Bala is largely a
ho-hum movie, Rolling Stone wrote:

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:41.860
"This Hollywoodized remake is mostly generic
and uninspired, but it also proves that Rodriguez

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:44.040
has the makings of a true movie star.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:48.720
It’ll be exciting to see what she does next…
so long as it’s not a sequel to this."

00:06:49.460 --> 00:06:54.500
2019's Hellboy reboot faced an uphill climb
from the start, and unfortunately it didn't

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.660
even come close to making its way to the top.

00:06:57.020 --> 00:07:02.440
With a worldwide gross of $21.8 million, the
movie failed to make up even half its production

00:07:02.440 --> 00:07:03.840
budget of $50 million.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.720
Hellboy's hype machine got off to a rocky
start.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:11.380
Fans reaction to the release of the film's
first trailer was mixed at best, and not even

00:07:11.380 --> 00:07:15.060
close to what any studio executive would want
for a superhero blockbuster.

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:19.360
In a sense, however, the reboot's toughest
competitors were the two previous Hellboy

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:22.900
movies directed by Guillermo del Toro, which
starred Ron Perlman.

00:07:23.520 --> 00:07:28.210
The shadow of Hellboy's predecessor was that
much darker for Perlman's very public regrets

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:31.300
over he and del Toro's failure to get their
own third Hellboy movie.

00:07:31.780 --> 00:07:36.100
And although he held no evident ill will for
new Hellboy David Harbour, Perlman wasn't

00:07:36.100 --> 00:07:39.770
shy about his disappointment; speaking to
Collider, he referred to someone else being

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:41.720
cast in the role as an "open wound."

00:07:42.310 --> 00:07:46.240
Considering the inherent difficulties in overcoming
these challenges, Hellboy would have needed

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:50.800
to be very good indeed to establish itself
as the basis for a revived franchise.

00:07:51.040 --> 00:07:52.080
Sadly, it wasn't.

00:07:52.440 --> 00:07:55.780
The Chicago Tribune warned readers Hellboy's
pacing is such that:

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:59.680
"...you don't so much watch this movie as
submit to being pummeled by it."

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:01.910
Meanwhile, Book &amp; Film Globe asked readers
to:

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:07.180
"...imagine del Toro's movies, except without
any spark, wit, fun, tension and excitement."

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:12.140
By all accounts, Hellboy is the kind of bad
film that invites a storm of brutal takedowns

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:16.840
— so much so that the London Evening Standard's
critic wrote that, if he were free to decide,

00:08:16.840 --> 00:08:17.340
he'd:

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:21.060
"...write nothing about the movie and leave
this space blank for readers' notes."

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:25.900
Peter Jackson's Lord of the Rings trilogy
made cinematic history, and even the less

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:30.230
well-received Hobbit movies made plenty of
money, but there's at least one J.R.R.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:34.440
Tolkien movie out there that didn't make a
splash — the one about the man himself.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:39.800
Starring Nicholas Hoult as Tolkien, and Lily
Collins as Tolkien's future wife Edith Bratt,

00:08:39.800 --> 00:08:43.959
Tolkien is about the author's early experiences
in school, how his life was rocked by the

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:47.920
outbreak of World War I, and how all those
experiences informed his writing.

00:08:48.170 --> 00:08:52.820
Tolkien earned an unimpressive $2.2 million
on its opening weekend, and hasn't gained

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.000
much ground since.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:59.760
As Forbes' review pointed out, as a biopic
without any A-list actors to support it, Tolkien

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:02.840
never really stood a chance of making it big
at the box office.

00:09:03.120 --> 00:09:06.300
Unfortunately, the critical response wasn't
much better, either.

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.140
Critics tended to think the movie was unimaginative,
unoriginal, and boring.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:15.171
For example, Salon's reviewer wrote that Tolkien
was doomed by a lack of vision, while The

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:19.240
Young Folks warned that the movie simply couldn't
escape the weight of its own tedium.

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:24.680
Poms is a comedy about a group of older women
in a retirement community who start up a competitive

00:09:24.680 --> 00:09:25.840
cheerleading squad.

00:09:26.209 --> 00:09:29.779
And that premise would be difficult enough
to pull off at the box office, even if the

00:09:29.780 --> 00:09:32.000
movie hadn't been faced with tremendous competition.

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:36.640
But Poms was released the same weekend as
Detective Pikachu and another all-female-led

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:37.940
comedy, The Hustle.

00:09:38.100 --> 00:09:42.020
It also faced Avengers: Endgame, which was
still busy breaking records when Poms was

00:09:42.020 --> 00:09:42.660
released.

00:09:43.029 --> 00:09:47.420
Factor in the skew towards an older audience,
who tend not to show up on opening weekends,

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:52.880
and the movie's limping opening weekend gross
of $5.6 million isn't that much of a surprise.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:57.380
Regardless of its target demographic or its
stiff competition, Poms' failure with the

00:09:57.400 --> 00:09:59.600
critics can't exactly have helped the movie's
chances.

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:03.839
With an embarrassing Rotten Tomatoes score
of 32%, the movie apparently showed off a

00:10:03.839 --> 00:10:08.800
great cast burdened with lazy writing — with
the star power of Diane Keaton and Jacki Weaver

00:10:08.800 --> 00:10:12.080
being simply not enough to save the movie
from box office oblivion.

00:10:13.740 --> 00:10:18.000
Based on Nicola Yoon's young adult novel of
the same name, The Sun Is Also a Star didn't

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.880
impress critics in the slightest.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:24.500
Reviewer consensus was that the teen drama
is poorly written, stretches believability,

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:25.760
and full of cliches.

00:10:26.209 --> 00:10:31.180
CNN called it "half-baked," The Observer called
it "contrived," while Jackie K. Cooper described

00:10:31.180 --> 00:10:33.200
it as "sappy to the nth degree."

00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:37.700
If nothing else, even the critics unimpressed
by the movie agree that the film's leads likely

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:41.980
have a bright future in Hollywood, but even
they couldn't save a seriously disappointing

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:42.580
script.

00:10:43.170 --> 00:10:48.260
These reviews likely contributed to the film's
lackluster opening weekend of $2.6 million,

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:50.520
across 2,073 screens.

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:54.460
Not only that, but the fact that The Sun Is
Also a Star was released the same weekend

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:59.610
as the incredibly successful John Wick: Chapter
3 may also have contributed to the teen romance's

00:10:59.610 --> 00:11:00.140
failure.

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:05.120
"You wanted me back - I'm back."

00:11:05.920 --> 00:11:07.840
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:08.000 --> 00:11:11.080
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:15.020
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

